realize() is a no-op on a realized graph (why the graph is rebuilt)
==============================================================================
  first realize()    143.461 ms   kernels compiled: 1
  realize() again       0.056 ms   kernels compiled: 0   <- no-op, this is the trap
  fresh graph          1.954 ms   kernels compiled: 0
  (a 'fresh graph' compiling 0 means tinygrad's on-disk cache already had
   the kernel, so the compile count is not the signal -- the TIME is:
   35x more than re-realizing, for identical work.)
